<title>USA: U.S. Spring/White Wheat-Spring and white bids up.</title>
<headline>U.S. Spring/White Wheat-Spring and white bids up.</headline>
<dateline>CHICAGO 1997-03-19</dateline>
<text>
<p>Spring wheat cash bids remained up on Wednesday in line with gains posted in MGE futures and underpinned by a lack of farm sales, dealers said.</p>
<p>&quot;With the (CBOT) board up, we are getting to a level where farmers are starting to take a little interest,&quot; a Minneapolis dealer said.</p>
<p>He said he believed wheat farmers were eyeing five to 10 cents over the MGE May contract as a target price. MGE spring wheat futures ended on the upside, with May climbing 5-1/2 cents to end at $4.07-1/4 a bushel.</p>
